Error: case_when() Missing TRUE


Problem


Show the code
bp_clean |&gt; 
  mutate(
    age_cat = case_when(
      age &lt; 40 ~ "Young",
      age &gt;= 60 ~ "Senior"
    )
  ) |&gt; 
  select(age, age_cat)


#&gt; # A tibble: 200 × 2
#&gt;      age age_cat
#&gt;    &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;chr&gt;  
#&gt;  1    36 Young  
#&gt;  2    79 Senior 
#&gt;  3    19 Young  
#&gt;  4    70 Senior 
#&gt;  5    61 Senior 
#&gt;  6    43 &lt;NA&gt;   
#&gt;  7    49 &lt;NA&gt;   
#&gt;  8    23 Young  
#&gt;  9    49 &lt;NA&gt;   
#&gt; 10    72 Senior 
#&gt; # ℹ 190 more rows



Solution


Show the code
bp_clean |&gt; 
  mutate(
    age_cat = case_when(
      age &lt; 40 ~ "Young",
      age &gt;= 60 ~ "Senior",
      TRUE ~ "Middle"
    )
  )

Functions and Control Flow

Functions are reusable blocks of code created with function()
Control flow uses if, else, for, while and repeat



Show the code
add &lt;- function(a, b) {
  result &lt;- a + b
  return(result)
}

if (add(2, 3) &gt; 4) {
  print("Yes, it is greater than 4")
}



Functions help organize logic and avoid repetition
Control flow enables conditional decisions and loops

Time series: decomposition

dengue &lt;- read_csv("../data/dengue_wards.csv", show_col_types = FALSE) |&gt;
  group_by(year, month) |&gt; summarise(cases = sum(cases), .groups = "drop")
s &lt;- stl(ts(dengue$cases, start = c(2023, 1), frequency = 12), s.window = "periodic")
as_tibble(s$time.series) |&gt; mutate(month = seq(as.Date("2023-01-01"), by = "month", length.out = n()), observed = dengue$cases) |&gt;
  pivot_longer(-month) |&gt; mutate(name = factor(name, c("observed", "trend", "seasonal", "remainder"))) |&gt;
  ggplot(aes(month, value)) + geom_line() + facet_wrap(~ name, ncol = 1, scales = "free_y") +
  labs(x = NULL, y = "Cases", title = "Observed = trend + seasonal + remainder")








stl() separates the seasonal monsoon peak from the slower trend; a large remainder points to an outbreak that the season alone does not explain.
